WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back, everybody!

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.634
We are hanging out
with John Oliver!

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:05.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:09.267
Now, John, as talk-show hosts,

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:11.701
we have to be knowledgeable
on a wide variety of topics,

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:14.267
and we also need to be able
to think quickly on our feet.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:15.767
-Do we? Okay.
-Yes. With that in mind,

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.634
I thought it would be fun to
play a new game we call

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:19.000
"Ten in Twelve."
-Okay.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.667
-Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:23.434
-♪ Ten in Twelve ♪

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:24.934
-All right,
here's how this game works,

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:26.400
and thank you for always
playing something with us.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.901
-Yeah.
-We're gonna take turns

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:30.434
picking a card from this pile.
Each card has a category on it.

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:33.267
Could be anything -- types of
animals, names of TV shows.

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.367
Whatever.
Then we'll have 12 seconds

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:37.234
to name 10 things
in that category.

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:39.901
-Okay. You know the moment just
before you see a car crash?

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:43.133
-Is that where we are?
-We're in that moment right now.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:44.601
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:46.267
-All right. I think --
I think this could be fun.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.801
-Okay. Okay, sure.
-10 in 12.

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:48.868
-We'll see about that.
-All right, here we go.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:50.133
-So, you go first.
-I will go first.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:51.434
-10 in 12.
-Yeah, okay.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.667
-What's your category?
-My category is first names.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:54.667
I can do this.
-Okay.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:55.934
-10 first names
in 12 seconds.

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.334
Ready?
-Yeah.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:01:03.200
-John, Jack, James, Jasper,
Jamie, Samantha, Steven...

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.901
-There are other letters.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:09.434
-...Terry, Larry, and Ted.

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:10.834
[ Dings ]
No?

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:12.033
-Did he get it?
-No, what did I do?

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:14.601
-Did you get it?
[ Dings ]

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:15.934
-Did I do it?
-I lost --

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:17.400
-I got 10!
All right, good.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.300
Harder than you think.
This game's harder --

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.801
Now "Family Feud"
seems really difficult.

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:25.934
-I'm more embarrassed by the
fact I genuinely lost count.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:28.501
-And it was only going
1 through 10.

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:29.734
-I thought I was doing 15.
Okay.

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:31.000
-Well done.
-All right, thank you.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.434
-Okay.
-You are up.

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.033
Just tell us the category, and
then whenever you're ready,

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.234
that's when we
start the countdown.

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:37.701
-Um, okay.
Holidays.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.834
-Okay.
10 holi-- that's hard.

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:41.033
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
-Ooh!

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:45.167
This is an audience that has
no faith in me whatsoever.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:46.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.701
-All right.
10 holidays in 12 seconds.

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:51.701
Whenever you're ready.
-Kwanzaa, President's Day,

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:55.934
MLK Day, Labor Day, my birthday,
your birthday,

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:58.234
Questlove's birthday,
Tariq's birthday...

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:00.400
-Oh, my God.
-Is that not a holiday?

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.434
Christmas, Hanukkah.
[ Buzzer ]

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.133
-Yeah, I think --
[ Dings ]

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:07.000
-Wait.
You got a buzz and a ding.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
I think he did it.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.267
Yes, you did it.
That was right down to the wire.

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:13.000
-There was --

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.334
-There was
four birthdays in there.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.667
-As long as you're not --
As long as you're willing

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:20.067
to not deny that the...
-Our birthdays are holidays.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:21.834
-...that birthdays of members
of your staff

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.634
are worth celebrating,
then I'm fine.

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.601
-No, I would never --
I would never, ever do that.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.100
-That's what I presumed.
So, I think we're good.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.133
Happy birthday, by the way.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:29.834
Questlove,
his birthday's this week.

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:30.968
There we go.
-Happy birthday.

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:33.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Happy birthday.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.267
-Let's do another round.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:35.968
-Happy birthday to all
who celebrate birthdays.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:38.300
-All who celebrate birthdays.
-Yeah.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.567
-All right, mine's
words that begin with "B."

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:42.701
-Wars that begin with "B"?
-No, words.

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:45.133
-Oh, I thought you said wars.
-No, not wars.

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:47.767
-I was like, the Boer War.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:48.868
-Okay. Okay.
-No.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.000
Words.
-Words.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.801
-Words that begin with "B."
Here we go.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:56.534
Uh, uh, uh,
balls, bat, bastard...

00:02:56.534 --> 00:03:05.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.067
[ Buzzer ]
-Stop.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:07.667
Don't do another one.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:11.834
Don't.
[ Sad tuba ]

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:14.234
Oh, man.
Oh, God, that is --

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:15.367
-That's all
I could come up with.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:16.767
-There is nothing
I'm happier with

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:20.000
than the nice guy, Jimmy Fallon,
the crack in that,

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.868
all it takes is just name three
words beginning with "B."

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.334
Bastard!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:26.767
-I couldn't think of --
-What about "M"?

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:31.200
I guess, uh, mouse, mistletoe,
mother [bleep]

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:37.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.000
-It doesn't take me --
doesn't take me much to crack.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.400
Hard to crack the shell, man.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.100
-I think -- I think yours have
been easier than mine.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:46.434
-Holidays is tough.
Yeah, words that begin with "B."

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:48.167
-Okay, all right.
Ready?

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:51.100
-Yes.
-Parts of the body.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.400
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.133
-Okay.
I got this, I got this.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.200
-Yes.
-Ready?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.000
-Yes.
-Toes, feet, ankles, shins,

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:04.033
knees, thighs, hips, hands,
fingers, elbows, shoulders.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:05.334
[ Dings ]
Yes.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:09.167
-You cheated!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:11.434
All right, that was good.
A little -- that was -- yeah.

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:12.534
[ Air horn ]
A little cheating there.

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:14.334
Yeah.
Okay.

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:15.601
This next round --
this is the last round.

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:16.834
We're down to the final round.
-Yes.

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:17.968
-Okay?
-Yeah.

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:19.367
-We're gonna
switch things up here, okay?

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:20.968
We're gonna join forces
to see if we can name

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:22.467
10 things together.
-Oh, yeah?

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:24.100
-Okay? Yeah, yeah.
-We're playing as a team now.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.868
-Okay.
-Okay? And if we get 10 --

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:28.534
-Who's going first?
You serve, or I serve?

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.601
-I think you serve,
because you're my guest.

00:04:30.601 --> 00:04:32.334
-Oh, thank you, Jimmy.
-Well, thanks for being here.

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:33.901
-I appreciate it.
-All right.

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:35.300
We get 10...
-Okay.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.067
-...we're both champions.
And we win -- we win everything.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:41.968
-Colors.
-Colors. We got this.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.834
-We have to --
We have to get this.

00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:45.300
-No, we have to get 10 colors.
-We have to get 10.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.334
Okay. Ready?
-Yes.

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:48.033
-Okay. Don't.
Okay.

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:49.234
Black.
-Blue.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:50.567
-Red.
-Yellow.

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:51.901
-White.
-Green.

00:04:51.901 --> 00:04:53.901
-Pink.
-Lavender.

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:57.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.434 --> 00:04:59.534
-Taupe.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:01.000
-Mauve.
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-We didn't get it?

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:05.767
-We didn't get 10?
[ Dings ]

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.100
Yes!
We got 10!

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.601
Mauve!
-We got it?

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:09.901
-Mauve! We got it.
-We got it?

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:11.868
-Mauve was the last color.
-Is --

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:14.901
-Is mauve a color?
-Is taupe a color?

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:17.000
[ Dings ]
Yes? Mauve is a color?

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.300
Yes!
Look at us!

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Never in doubt.

00:05:19.567 --> 00:05:21.234
-John Oliver, everybody!
-Never in doubt.

00:05:21.234 --> 00:05:22.901
-"Last Week Tonight
with John Oliver"

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:26.133
returns for its 10th season,
Sunday, February 19th,

00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:28.634
11:00 p.m., on HBO/HBO Max.

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:31.133
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

